course: dictionary
lesson: 6288
title: One word, many moods
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word mood has three meanings. First, it is how someone feels at a particular time, such as happy, grumpy or calm. «Taking breaks from screens and playing outside helps your mood.» Here mood means how you feel inside.
explain: Second, mood is the feeling of a place, story or piece of music. «Setting openings can build mood, but a long list of things in the sky and on the ground slows a story down.» Writers create a mood with words, weather and setting, so the reader feels spooky, calm or happy.
explain: Third, "in the mood for" means wanting to do something. The phrase "in a good mood" means feeling cheerful, and "in a bad mood" means feeling cross or fed up. A mood swing is a quick change from one mood to another.
fact: Mood means how someone feels at a particular time.
fact: Mood can also mean the feeling of a place, story or piece of music.
fact: «In the mood for» means wanting to do something, such as «in the mood for a walk».
fact: «Too little sleep makes it harder to concentrate, learn and stay in a good mood.» Sleep, food, exercise and friends can change your mood.
fact: To check the meaning, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Too little sleep makes it harder to concentrate, learn and stay in a good mood.» What does mood mean here? | *How someone feels at a particular time | A kind of music with a fast beat | A list of things to do | A type of weather
exercise: The music had a spooky mood. What does mood mean in this sentence? | A long list of things in the sky | *The feeling of a place, story or piece of music | A tired, grumpy person | A wish to go outside
exercise: Mia says, "I'm in the mood for a walk." What does "in the mood for" mean? | Losing a game | Feeling very sick | *Wanting to do something | Being very tall
test: «Setting openings can build mood, but a long list of things in the sky and on the ground slows a story down.» In this sentence, what does mood most likely mean? | A kind of sleep | A list of things in the sky | A walk in the park | *The feeling a story creates
test: What is a mood swing? | A slow walk in the park | A long, deep sleep | *A quick change from one mood to another | A type of screen
exam: «Too much screen time can affect mood and sleep.» Which check shows the meaning of mood? | *Swap in how you feel, and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters in mood | Ignore the words around it | Look only at the word before mood
